From c00181235df53c9d8bbb78b06b887d5872171fe0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bruno Pires <bruno@blastersystems.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:16:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 123/124] glm cuda: TF_GLM_ROCE_MULTI=1 lends the small
 all-gathers to fabric/tp's multirank RoCE at three ranks or more (upstream
 port)

Ported onto f350cd3 + patches 0001-0122 from upstream ashhart/TensorFold:
  1911e7bc3 build: GLM's CUDA family takes fabric/tp over the engine's own cuda module
  81e25bb55 cuda tp_group: three ranks or more can borrow a wire for small all-gathers, every rank or none
  b99c48a53 glm cuda: TF_GLM_ROCE_MULTI, a setting every rank must share before any opens the borrowed wire
  65ec7eadd glm cuda: TF_GLM_ROCE_MULTI=1 lends the main stream's small all-gathers to fabric/tp's multirank RoCE, every rank or none
  1e9975556 glm cuda: the probe's vote is lendIfAll, with a test that one rank's mismatch keeps every rank on NCCL
  ed20c5be4 glm cuda: the probe is ready on every rank before any enters a gather, and a failed NCCL gather or wait refuses

Opt-in, off by default; a no-op under three ranks. At world 3 every all-gather is NCCL's: the two-rank RoCE path is
world 2 only and patch 0108's ring world 4 only. With the switch every rank opens fabric/tp's multirank RoCE (a queue
pair to every peer; its mailbox kernel from TF_TP_KERNEL_IMAGE, its bootstrap at TF_TP_MASTER), probes one 4 KiB
gather against NCCL's, and lends the wire to the group only when every rank's bytes matched; one rank failing keeps
every rank on NCCL (TF_TP_ROCE_FALLBACK=error refuses instead). Gathers larger than the mailbox slot
(TF_TP_MAILBOX_MAX_KB) stay on NCCL, so prompt chunks keep their route. Upstream measured at TP=3 on three GB10s:
decode 51.2 -> 52.6 tok/s with drafts, a cold 136k prompt 1.2-1.6% slower.

Recipe-side merges:
- tp_group.zig carries 0034's peer-store gather and 0108's ring beside upstream's Multi: allGather tries p2p, fast,
  ring, multi, then NCCL; closeWires closes all four; abort reaches p2p and multi.
- Settings and fingerprint layout 18 -> 19 (roce_multi); the refusal without TF_TP_MASTER / TF_TP_KERNEL_IMAGE sits
  beside 0122's kda_pad one.
